==Swedish==

===Etymology===
{{suf|sv|tumme|t1=thumb|a}}

===Verb===
{{sv-verb-reg}}

# to [[thumb]] (touch or manipulate with one's thumb)
# to confirm mutual agreement (sometimes by parties pressing their right thumbs against each other), to [[shake on it]], to [[pinky swear]]
#: {{ux|sv|Vi '''tummade''' på det|We '''shook''' on it}}
# {{senseid|sv|compromise on}} to slightly [[compromise]] on, to [[skimp]] on (something)
#: {{ux|sv|De '''tummade''' på säkerheten|They '''compromised''' / '''skimped''' on security}}
# {{lb|sv|chiefly|historical}} to [[measure]] (lumber) in [[inches]] ({{m|sv|tum}})

====Usage notes====
Close to synonymous with {{m|sv|avkall|göra avkall på}} in ({{senseno|sv|compromise on}}). Often of being willing to compromise on or play a bit fast and loose with something considered important, in a critical sense.

